Meaningless? All right, since I spent around thirty hours and several
other near-attempts (none of which were rerolled) trying for an under
- 20K ascension, I'll bite. Chuckcar, even if you were correct, that
was one of the rudest, most condescending posts I've ever read on
RGRN. And you were far from correct, as evidenced by several notable
YAAPs, one of which was referenced on Wikihack itself, that relied on
start-scumming more than I did.

There is a fundamental difference between reroll scummers who scum for
outstanding equipment instead of playing normally and conduct players
who want to achieve some difficult requirement. The former are using
rerolling as a crutch. The latter simply don't want to wade through
200 characters with a 99% mortality rate to get one with a ring of
slow digestion for foodless, or spellbook of sleep. They aren't
adjusting their playing style to expect a ring of conflict, magic
marker, and fountain wish from the get-go.

Admittedly, "fast" is a far less demanding conduct than "foodless" or
"athiest" or Tenaya's incredible set of *ten* conducts. But magic
marker (20% for a wiz) is far less restrictive of a starting
requirement than "ring of slow digestion" (around 6% I think), too.
Each of the other speed runs referenced on Wikihack was the result of
some player getting either excellent starting equipment or an early
game wand of wishing. They weren't playing a ton of normal Wizards in
a bunch of botched speed-run attempts like you heavy-handedly seem to
expect. Notably, I *did* play a bunch of wizards to the death, some of
which made the quest and castle, and scummed on the last one.

Sure, it isn't particularly noteworthy in comparison to other speed
runs, but it's still a speed run, and it's still an ascension. I don't
really have time to play this game in the first place, and getting
branded as a common cheater who hasn't learned to play without a ton
of early fountain wishes and cool toys after *eleven ascensions* (wiz
x 4, pri, rog, hea, kni, arc, tou, bar) is more than I can stand.
Chuckcar, why don't you go tell Tenaya that his ten-conduct ascension
was "meaningless" because he wanted to start with Sleep? Break the
news to all the foodless cheaters who started with =SD? If you aren't
willing to do that, I suggest you retract your post. Otherwise, I
still suggest you retract it because you accused me of "save
